IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `scja-core`

-- scja2-part5-ca-capital-defs.l4: Part 5 (Court of Appeal), Division 4, Post-appeal application in capital case and finding of abuse of process: s 60F, the definitions of the Division.
-- Supreme Court of Judicature Act 1969 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from 1 July 2024.
-- The source is a plain-text rendering (SCJA1969.txt), not the official text. Layer 1: the law, objectively; every name begins with the label of its provision.
-- Encoded for the prisoner awaiting capital punishment (the PACP) as the individual on whom the court acts; there is no seat export for this Division.
-- Section 60F opens "unless the context otherwise requires": that is a fork (NOTES.md); each definition below is read as the text states it.
-- A "means" definition answers JUST FALSE where its conditions are not met (the text says no in its own words); a bare list with no "only" answers NOTHING (ruling of 2026-10-29).
-- Borrowed facts (the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 and the Constitution are not among the sources) are asked as plain yes/no inputs.

§ `Part 5, Division 4 -- Post-appeal application in capital case and finding of abuse of process`

§§ `s 60F -- Interpretation of this Division`

-- src:3462 | 60F. In this Division, unless the context otherwise requires —
@ref s 60F chapeau (src:3462)
GIVEN `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60F chapeau the definitions of this Division apply in this use` MEANS
    IF `the context otherwise requires`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this Division, unless the context otherwise requires" -- the "unless" is met, so the definitions do not apply in this use
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:3464 | “application for PACC permission” means an application for
-- src:3465 | permission to make a PACC application;
@ref s 60F "application for PACC permission" (src:3464-3465)
GIVEN `it is an application for permission to make a PACC application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60F "application for PACC permission" the application is an application for PACC permission` MEANS
    IF `it is an application for permission to make a PACC application`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'application for PACC permission' means an application for permission to make a PACC application"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:3467 | “application for review permission” means an application for
-- src:3468 | permission to make a review application;
@ref s 60F "application for review permission" (src:3467-3468)
GIVEN `it is an application for permission to make a review application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60F "application for review permission" the application is an application for review permission` MEANS
    IF `it is an application for permission to make a review application`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'application for review permission' means an application for permission to make a review application"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:3470 | “counsel” means any advocate and solicitor;
@ref s 60F "counsel" (src:3470)
GIVEN role IS A Role
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60F "counsel" the person is counsel` MEANS
    IF role EQUALS `Advocate and solicitor`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'counsel' means any advocate and solicitor"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:3472 | “Judge of the Court of Appeal” means a Judge sitting in the
-- src:3473 | Court of Appeal in accordance with this Act and the
-- src:3474 | Constitution;
@ref s 60F "Judge of the Court of Appeal" (src:3472-3474)
GIVEN `the Judge is sitting in the Court of Appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Judge sits in accordance with this Act and the Constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60F "Judge of the Court of Appeal" the Judge is a Judge of the Court of Appeal` MEANS
    IF `the Judge is sitting in the Court of Appeal` AND `the Judge sits in accordance with this Act and the Constitution`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'Judge of the Court of Appeal' means a Judge sitting in the Court of Appeal in accordance with this Act and the Constitution"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:3476 | “PACP” means a prisoner awaiting capital punishment;
@ref s 60F "PACP" (src:3476)
GIVEN `the person is a prisoner awaiting capital punishment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60F "PACP" the person is a PACP` MEANS
    IF `the person is a prisoner awaiting capital punishment`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'PACP' means a prisoner awaiting capital punishment"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:3495 | Examples
-- src:3497 | Examples of an application made by a PACP the determination of
-- src:3498 | which calls into question, or may call into question, the propriety of the
-- src:3499 | conviction of, the imposition of the sentence of death on, or the carrying out
-- src:3500 | of the sentence of death on, the PACP are —
-- src:3502 | (a) an application challenging the President’s order;
-- src:3504 | (b) an application challenging the manner in which the death sentence
-- src:3505 | is to be carried out;
-- src:3507 | (c) an application challenging the imposition of the sentence of death
-- src:3508 | as a form of punishment (such as an application alleging that the
-- src:3515 | death penalty is an unlawful deprivation of life under Article 9(1)
-- src:3516 | of the Constitution);
-- src:3518 | (d) an application challenging the Public Prosecutor’s decision not to
-- src:3519 | certify that the PACP has substantively assisted the Central
-- src:3520 | Narcotics Bureau in disrupting drug trafficking activities within or
-- src:3521 | outside Singapore, under section 33B(2)(b) of the Misuse of
-- src:3522 | Drugs Act 1973; and
-- src:3524 | (e) an application challenging the Public Prosecutor’s decision to
-- src:3525 | institute and conduct proceedings against the PACP for an offence
-- src:3526 | punishable with death.
@ref s 60F Examples (src:3495-3526)
DECLARE `s 60F Examples kind of application` IS ONE OF
    `s 60F Examples(a) an application challenging the President's order`
    `s 60F Examples(b) an application challenging the manner in which the death sentence is to be carried out`
    `s 60F Examples(c) an application challenging the imposition of the sentence of death as a form of punishment`
    `s 60F Examples(d) an application challenging the Public Prosecutor's decision not to certify that the PACP has substantively assisted the Central Narcotics Bureau`
    `s 60F Examples(e) an application challenging the Public Prosecutor's decision to institute and conduct proceedings against the PACP for an offence punishable with death`
    `s 60F Examples another application`

-- src:3495 | Examples
-- src:3497 | Examples of an application made by a PACP the determination of
-- src:3498 | which calls into question, or may call into question, the propriety of the
-- src:3499 | conviction of, the imposition of the sentence of death on, or the carrying out
-- src:3500 | of the sentence of death on, the PACP are —
-- src:3502 | (a) an application challenging the President’s order;
-- src:3504 | (b) an application challenging the manner in which the death sentence
-- src:3505 | is to be carried out;
-- src:3507 | (c) an application challenging the imposition of the sentence of death
-- src:3508 | as a form of punishment (such as an application alleging that the
-- src:3515 | death penalty is an unlawful deprivation of life under Article 9(1)
-- src:3516 | of the Constitution);
-- src:3518 | (d) an application challenging the Public Prosecutor’s decision not to
-- src:3519 | certify that the PACP has substantively assisted the Central
-- src:3520 | Narcotics Bureau in disrupting drug trafficking activities within or
-- src:3521 | outside Singapore, under section 33B(2)(b) of the Misuse of
-- src:3522 | Drugs Act 1973; and
-- src:3524 | (e) an application challenging the Public Prosecutor’s decision to
-- src:3525 | institute and conduct proceedings against the PACP for an offence
-- src:3526 | punishable with death.
@ref s 60F Examples (src:3495-3526)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 60F Examples kind of application`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60F Examples the application is an example of an application made by a PACP whose determination calls into question the propriety of the conviction, the sentence or its carrying out` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 60F Examples(a) an application challenging the President's order` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 60F Examples(b) an application challenging the manner in which the death sentence is to be carried out` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 60F Examples(c) an application challenging the imposition of the sentence of death as a form of punishment` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 60F Examples(d) an application challenging the Public Prosecutor's decision not to certify that the PACP has substantively assisted the Central Narcotics Bureau` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 60F Examples(e) an application challenging the Public Prosecutor's decision to institute and conduct proceedings against the PACP for an offence punishable with death` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text gives "Examples" and does not close the list
    WHEN `s 60F Examples another application` THEN NOTHING

-- src:3489 | (ii) the determination of the application calls into
-- src:3490 | question, or may call into question, the
-- src:3491 | propriety of the conviction of, the imposition
-- src:3492 | of the sentence of death on, or the carrying out
-- src:3493 | of the sentence of death on, the PACP;
@ref s 60F "post-appeal application in a capital case"(b)(ii) (src:3489-3493)
GIVEN example IS A `s 60F Examples kind of application`
      `its determination otherwise calls into question, or may call into question, the propriety of the conviction of, the imposition of the sentence of death on, or the carrying out of the sentence of death on, the PACP` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 60F "post-appeal application in a capital case"(b)(ii) the determination calls into question the propriety of the conviction, the sentence or its carrying out` MEANS
    `s 60F Examples the application is an example of an application made by a PACP whose determination calls into question the propriety of the conviction, the sentence or its carrying out` example EQUALS JUST TRUE
    OR `its determination otherwise calls into question, or may call into question, the propriety of the conviction of, the imposition of the sentence of death on, or the carrying out of the sentence of death on, the PACP`

-- src:3478 | “post-appeal application in a capital case” or “PACC
-- src:3479 | application” means any application (not being a review
-- src:3480 | application) —
-- src:3482 | (a) made by a PACP after the relevant date; and
-- src:3484 | (b) to which either of the following applies:
-- src:3486 | (i) the application is for a stay of the execution of
-- src:3487 | the death sentence on the PACP;
-- src:3489 | (ii) the determination of the application calls into
-- src:3490 | question, or may call into question, the
-- src:3491 | propriety of the conviction of, the imposition
-- src:3492 | of the sentence of death on, or the carrying out
-- src:3493 | of the sentence of death on, the PACP;
@ref s 60F "post-appeal application in a capital case" (src:3478-3493)
GIVEN `it is a review application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made by a PACP` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 60F "relevant date" it is made after the relevant date` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `limb (b)(i): it is for a stay of the execution of the death sentence on the PACP` IS A BOOLEAN
      `limb (b)(ii): its determination calls into question the propriety` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60F "post-appeal application in a capital case" the application is a PACC application` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means any application (not being a review application)"
        IF `it is a review application` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means any application ... (a) made by a PACP"
        IF NOT `it is made by a PACP` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) to which either of the following applies" -- neither does
        IF NOT (`limb (b)(i): it is for a stay of the execution of the death sentence on the PACP` OR `limb (b)(ii): its determination calls into question the propriety`) THEN JUST FALSE
        -- the definition then turns on "after the relevant date" (paragraph (a)): the answer of the "relevant date" definition is passed through
        OTHERWISE `s 60F "relevant date" it is made after the relevant date`

-- src:3528 | “President’s order”, in relation to a PACP, means the order of the
-- src:3529 | President under section 313(1)(f) of the Criminal Procedure
-- src:3530 | Code 2010 stating that the sentence of death is to be carried
-- src:3531 | out against the PACP;
@ref s 60F "President's order" (src:3528-3531)
GIVEN `it is the order of the President under section 313(1)(f) of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 stating that the sentence of death is to be carried out against the PACP` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60F "President's order" the order is the President's order` MEANS
    IF `it is the order of the President under section 313(1)(f) of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 stating that the sentence of death is to be carried out against the PACP`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'President's order', in relation to a PACP, means the order of the President under section 313(1)(f) of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 stating that the sentence of death is to be carried out against the PACP"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:3533 | “relevant application” means —
-- src:3535 | (a) an application for PACC permission;
-- src:3537 | (b) a PACC application;
-- src:3539 | (c) an application for review permission; or
-- src:3541 | (d) a review application;
@ref s 60F "relevant application" (src:3533-3541)
DECLARE `s 60F "relevant application" kind of application` IS ONE OF
    `s 60F "relevant application"(a) an application for PACC permission`
    `s 60F "relevant application"(b) a PACC application`
    `s 60F "relevant application"(c) an application for review permission`
    `s 60F "relevant application"(d) a review application`
    `s 60F "relevant application" another application`

-- src:3533 | “relevant application” means —
-- src:3535 | (a) an application for PACC permission;
-- src:3537 | (b) a PACC application;
-- src:3539 | (c) an application for review permission; or
-- src:3541 | (d) a review application;
@ref s 60F "relevant application" (src:3533-3541)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 60F "relevant application" kind of application`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60F "relevant application" the application is a relevant application` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 60F "relevant application"(a) an application for PACC permission` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 60F "relevant application"(b) a PACC application` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 60F "relevant application"(c) an application for review permission` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 60F "relevant application"(d) a review application` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'relevant application' means (a) ... (b) ... (c) ...; or (d) ..."
    WHEN `s 60F "relevant application" another application` THEN JUST FALSE

-- src:3543 | “relevant date” means —
-- src:3545 | (a) in relation to the first PACC application by a
-- src:3546 | PACP —
-- src:3548 | (i) the date of dismissal of the appeal by the Court
-- src:3549 | of Appeal (whether before, on or after the date
-- src:3550 | of commencement of the Post‑appeal
-- src:3551 | Applications in Capital Cases Act 2022) in
-- src:3552 | relation to the offence for which the sentence of
-- src:3553 | death was imposed on the PACP;
-- src:3555 | (ii) the date of imposition of the sentence of death
-- src:3556 | by the Court of Appeal (whether before, on or
-- src:3557 | after the date of commencement of the
-- src:3558 | Post‑appeal Applications in Capital Cases
-- src:3559 | Act 2022) in an appeal against the acquittal
-- src:3560 | of the PACP of an offence punishable with
-- src:3567 | death, or against a non‑capital sentence
-- src:3568 | imposed on the PACP; or
-- src:3570 | (iii) the date of the issuance by the Court of Appeal
-- src:3571 | of a certificate (whether before, on or after the
-- src:3572 | date of commencement of the Post‑appeal
-- src:3573 | Applications in Capital Cases Act 2022)
-- src:3574 | confirming the imposition of the sentence of
-- src:3575 | death on the PACP; and
-- src:3577 | (b) in relation to the second or any subsequent PACC
-- src:3578 | application (called the instant application) by a
-- src:3579 | PACP —
-- src:3581 | (i) the date mentioned in paragraph (a); or
-- src:3583 | (ii) if prior to the making of the instant application,
-- src:3584 | there has been a determination of —
-- src:3586 | (A) any application for PACC permission
-- src:3587 | (not being an application for PACC
-- src:3588 | permission for the instant application); or
-- src:3590 | (B) any PACC application,
-- src:3592 | (ii) in relation to the PACP, the date of the most
-- src:3593 | recent of any such determination;
@ref s 60F "relevant date" (src:3543-3593)
GIVEN `it is the first PACC application by the PACP` IS A BOOLEAN
      `limb (a)(i): the date of dismissal of the appeal by the Court of Appeal in relation to the offence for which the sentence of death was imposed on the PACP` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `limb (a)(ii): the date of imposition of the sentence of death by the Court of Appeal in an appeal against the acquittal of the PACP of an offence punishable with death, or against a non-capital sentence` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `limb (a)(iii): the date of the issuance by the Court of Appeal of a certificate confirming the imposition of the sentence of death on the PACP` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `limb (b)(ii): the date of the most recent determination, before the instant application, of an earlier application for PACC permission or PACC application` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 60F "relevant date" the relevant date` MEANS
    -- paragraph (a): exactly one of the three dates (i), (ii), (iii) applies to a PACP; the text does not say which prevails if more than one is stated
    LET `the date under paragraph (a)` MEANS
        CONSIDER `limb (a)(i): the date of dismissal of the appeal by the Court of Appeal in relation to the offence for which the sentence of death was imposed on the PACP`
        WHEN JUST dismissal THEN
            CONSIDER `limb (a)(ii): the date of imposition of the sentence of death by the Court of Appeal in an appeal against the acquittal of the PACP of an offence punishable with death, or against a non-capital sentence`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN
                CONSIDER `limb (a)(iii): the date of the issuance by the Court of Appeal of a certificate confirming the imposition of the sentence of death on the PACP`
                WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST dismissal
                -- NOTHING-kind (silent): two of the three dates are stated and the text does not say which prevails
                WHEN JUST certificate THEN NOTHING
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): two of the three dates are stated and the text does not say which prevails
            WHEN JUST imposition THEN NOTHING
        WHEN NOTHING THEN
            CONSIDER `limb (a)(ii): the date of imposition of the sentence of death by the Court of Appeal in an appeal against the acquittal of the PACP of an offence punishable with death, or against a non-capital sentence`
            WHEN JUST imposition THEN
                CONSIDER `limb (a)(iii): the date of the issuance by the Court of Appeal of a certificate confirming the imposition of the sentence of death on the PACP`
                WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST imposition
                -- NOTHING-kind (silent): two of the three dates are stated and the text does not say which prevails
                WHEN JUST certificate THEN NOTHING
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): none of the three dates (a)(i), (ii), (iii) is stated
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `limb (a)(iii): the date of the issuance by the Court of Appeal of a certificate confirming the imposition of the sentence of death on the PACP`
    IN
        IF `it is the first PACC application by the PACP`
        THEN `the date under paragraph (a)`
        ELSE
            -- paragraph (b), read as: if there has been a determination before the instant application, its date, otherwise the date mentioned in paragraph (a) (fork F60F-1, NOTES.md)
            CONSIDER `limb (b)(ii): the date of the most recent determination, before the instant application, of an earlier application for PACC permission or PACC application`
            WHEN JUST latest THEN JUST latest
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `the date under paragraph (a)`

-- src:3543 | “relevant date” means —
-- src:3545 | (a) in relation to the first PACC application by a
-- src:3546 | PACP —
-- src:3548 | (i) the date of dismissal of the appeal by the Court
-- src:3549 | of Appeal (whether before, on or after the date
-- src:3550 | of commencement of the Post‑appeal
-- src:3551 | Applications in Capital Cases Act 2022) in
-- src:3552 | relation to the offence for which the sentence of
-- src:3553 | death was imposed on the PACP;
-- src:3555 | (ii) the date of imposition of the sentence of death
-- src:3556 | by the Court of Appeal (whether before, on or
-- src:3557 | after the date of commencement of the
-- src:3558 | Post‑appeal Applications in Capital Cases
-- src:3559 | Act 2022) in an appeal against the acquittal
-- src:3560 | of the PACP of an offence punishable with
-- src:3567 | death, or against a non‑capital sentence
-- src:3568 | imposed on the PACP; or
-- src:3570 | (iii) the date of the issuance by the Court of Appeal
-- src:3571 | of a certificate (whether before, on or after the
-- src:3572 | date of commencement of the Post‑appeal
-- src:3573 | Applications in Capital Cases Act 2022)
-- src:3574 | confirming the imposition of the sentence of
-- src:3575 | death on the PACP; and
-- src:3577 | (b) in relation to the second or any subsequent PACC
-- src:3578 | application (called the instant application) by a
-- src:3579 | PACP —
-- src:3581 | (i) the date mentioned in paragraph (a); or
-- src:3583 | (ii) if prior to the making of the instant application,
-- src:3584 | there has been a determination of —
-- src:3586 | (A) any application for PACC permission
-- src:3587 | (not being an application for PACC
-- src:3588 | permission for the instant application); or
-- src:3590 | (B) any PACC application,
-- src:3592 | (ii) in relation to the PACP, the date of the most
-- src:3593 | recent of any such determination;
@ref s 60F "relevant date" (src:3543-3593)
GIVEN `the date on which the application is made` IS A DATE
      `the relevant date` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60F "relevant date" it is made after the relevant date` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the relevant date`
    -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the relevant date cannot be worked out from the facts given
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST d THEN
        IF `the date on which the application is made` GREATER THAN d
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) made by a PACP after the relevant date" -- it is made on or before that date
        ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:3595 | “review application” means a review application within the
-- src:3596 | meaning of section 394F of the Criminal Procedure
-- src:3597 | Code 2010 where the application is to review an earlier
-- src:3598 | decision of the Court of Appeal relating to the offence for
-- src:3599 | which the sentence of death was imposed on a PACP.
@ref s 60F "review application" (src:3595-3599)
GIVEN `it is a review application within the meaning of section 394F of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is to review an earlier decision of the Court of Appeal relating to the offence for which the sentence of death was imposed on a PACP` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60F "review application" the application is a review application` MEANS
    IF `it is a review application within the meaning of section 394F of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010` AND `it is to review an earlier decision of the Court of Appeal relating to the offence for which the sentence of death was imposed on a PACP`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'review application' means a review application within the meaning of section 394F of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 where the application is to review an earlier decision of the Court of Appeal relating to the offence for which the sentence of death was imposed on a PACP"
    ELSE JUST FALSE
